>
> As per our Tri-Agency Guide on Financial Administration (TAGFA), expenses
> incurred after the termination of a grant are not eligible. This
> encompasses travel for a grantee in the case the travel has not occurred.
>
>
>
> *Outstanding commitment:* an outstanding commitment (unpaid invoice)
> occurs when the grant recipient, or administering institution, has receiv=
ed
> a good or service before the end date of the grant or, if applicable,
> within the ATUF period of the grant and the invoice for the good or servi=
ce
> was not paid within that timeline.
>
>
>
> *Pre-payment for the cost of a good or service that will be provided afte=
r
> the end date of the grant=E2=80=94or, if applicable, the ATUF period of t=
he
> grant=E2=80=94is not classified as an outstanding commitment. The pre-pay=
ment is an
> ineligible cost as the good or service was provided after the grant end
> date.*
>
>
>
> The Agencies may authorize a phase-out period of up to six months from th=
e
> termination date to settle outstanding eligible commitments or
> expenditures.
>
>
>
> If the term of a commitment extends beyond the phase-out period, the
> committed costs incurred beyond the phase-out period are the administerin=
g
> institution=E2=80=99s responsibility.
>
>
>
> If a phase-out period is not authorized, the administering institution is
> responsible for all outstanding commitments or expenditures.
>
>
>
> However, I have sent your request to management to see if an exception ca=
n
> be made in your case. I will follow up with the results shortly.
>
>
